==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rouseabout}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|roust|about}}.<ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|US}} An [[unskilled]] [[laborer]], especially at an [[oilfield]], at a [[circus]] or on a [[ship]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|rouser|rousie|rouster|;|roughneck}}
#* {{RQ:Lewis Babbitt|chapter=14|passage=The U. is my own Alma Mater, and I am proud to be known as an alumni, but there are certain instructors there who seem to think we ought to turn the conduct of the nation over to hoboes and '''roustabouts'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1961|translator=w:Robert Fitzgerald|author=w:Homer|title=w:Odyssey|location=New York|publisher=Farrar, Straus & Giroux|section=Book Eleven, 668-9
|passage=Then Sísiphos in torment I beheld / being '''roustabout''' to a tremendous boulder.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1974|author=w:Saul Bellow|chapter=Him with His Foot in His Mouth|title=Collected Stories|page=377|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2001
|passage=Brooklyn Tony, who had run away from home to be a circus '''roustabout''', became a poster artist and eventually an Abstract Expressionist.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=7 January 2013|author=Celeste Headlee|journal=w:NPR|url=http://corpus.byu.edu/coca/|passage=She works in McGregor, North Dakota as a '''roustabout''' pusher. That means she and her crew help fix and maintain the drilling sites.|accessdate=30 April 2019|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20151029175217/http://corpus.byu.edu/coca/|archivedate=29 October 2015}}
#* See also quotations under [[rouseabout]].

